      "title": "Fix locale-dependent git repo detection",
      "body": "Fixes #1089\n\n## Root cause\n`tea clone` initializes the command context by probing the current directory with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`. `classifyRepoError` recognizes the \"not a git repository\" case by matching the English stderr text. When git emits localized errors (for example with `LANG=de_DE.UTF-8`), that match fails, and the otherwise harmless \"no repo here\" error is returned as fatal before cloning.\n\n## Fix\nPin the locale of git subprocesses to `C` by overriding `LC_ALL`, `LANG`, and `LANGUAGE` in `runGitCommand`. This keeps all git output stable for parsing while leaving the parent process locale untouched.\n\n## Tests\nAdded a regression test using a fake git executable that emits a German \"not a repository\" error unless the locale is forced to `C`, and verifies `ErrRepositoryNotExists` is returned.",
